   AWS Console Step-by-Step (Screenshot Style) –
         Instance Refresh Zero Downtime:

Step 1: Go to EC2 Console
          AWS Console → Services → EC2
          Left Menu → Launch Templates
          Select your template
          Click → Actions → Create new version

Update:

- AMI ID (latest patched)

- Instance config if needed

- Save new version

Step 2: Update Auto Scaling Group

          EC2 → Auto Scaling Groups
          Select your ASG
          Click → Edit
          Scroll → Launch Template
          Select → Latest Version
          Click → Update

Step 3: Start Instance Refresh

          Inside ASG:
          Go to → Instance Refresh tab
          Click → Start Instance Refresh

Configuration Screen (Important):

          Minimum Healthy Percentage: 100
          Maximum Healthy Percentage: 200
          Instance Warm-up: 180 seconds
          Click → Start Refresh

Step 4: What You Will See (Live Flow)

          Activity Tab:

          Launching new EC2 instance...
          Instance entering InService...
          ECS agent connecting...
          Target group health check passing...

Then:
          Terminating old instance...

Step 5: Verify in ECS

          ECS → Cluster → Services
          Check:
          - New tasks starting
          - Old tasks stopping
          - No drop in running count

Step 6: Verify in ALB

          EC2 → Target Groups → Targets tab
          Check:
          - New instances → healthy
          - Old instances → draining → removed

Failure Scenario Screen
        If health check fails:

        Status: Failed
        Reason: Health check failed

        Action:
        - Fix AMI / App issue
        - Restart refresh

Final Result

- All EC2 instances replaced

- Traffic uninterrupted

- Zero downtime achieved
